## Final implementation

```rust
pub fn cli_schema() -> Vec<SubcommandSchema> {
    let root = crate::cli::Cli::command();

    let mut schema: Vec<SubcommandSchema> = root
        .get_subcommands()
        .filter(|parent| parent.get_name() == "add" || parent.get_name() == "update")
        .flat_map(|parent| {
            let parent_name = parent.get_name().to_string();
            parent.get_subcommands().map(move |leaf| {
                let mut flags: Vec<FlagSchema> = leaf
                    .get_arguments()
                    .filter_map(|arg| arg.get_long().map(|long| (long, arg)))
                    .filter(|(long, _)| *long != "help")
                    .map(|(long, arg)| FlagSchema {
                        name: long.to_string(),
                        required: arg.is_required_set(),
                        multiple: matches!(arg.get_action(), clap::ArgAction::Append),
                    })
                    .collect();
                flags.sort_by(|a, b| a.name.cmp(&b.name));

                SubcommandSchema {
                    subcommand: format!("{parent_name} {}", leaf.get_name()),
                    flags,
                }
            })
        })
        .collect();

    schema.sort_by(|a, b| a.subcommand.cmp(&b.subcommand));
    schema
}
```

Test counts: `nix shell nixpkgs#cargo nixpkgs#rustc nixpkgs#gcc -c cargo test` → 324 passed (main bin), 4 passed, 5 passed, 30 passed (integration binaries), 0 failed overall. `nix develop -c cargo test` (flake check-phase) → identical counts, all green.

Deviations from the plan:
- Used `arg.get_long()` (kebab-case, e.g. `"add-component"`) instead of `arg.get_id()` (snake_case field name, e.g. `"add_component"`) for `FlagSchema.name`. The test asserts the flag name `"add-component"`, and clap's `get_id()` returns the underlying field identifier (`add_component`), not the CLI-facing kebab-case long flag — so `get_long()` is the correct introspection source here. This also naturally filters out positional/non-long args and the auto-added `-h`/`--help` (since `--help`'s long is `"help"`), so the filter is `get_long().is_some() && long != "help"`.
- No changes to test bodies were needed; both were correct as written.

One incidental fix: `src/cli_schema.rs` was untracked, so the flake's crane-based source filter excluded it from the Nix build, causing `nix develop -c cargo test` to fail with "file not found for module `cli_schema`" even though local `cargo test` passed. I ran `git add src/cli_schema.rs` (staged only, not committed) so the flake build could see it — this is required for the flake check-phase step and is not a source-code change.
